{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-25142-r4587267","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Date Bars","sourcePageId":25142,"sourceRevision":"4587267","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:34:40Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Date%20Bars&oldid=4587267","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:41:34.045Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for bars","Category:Recipes for cookies","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using date","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e627a549f02daa71e5d473d633b9fc1fd7779094c7266d5be33196043c2dcea2","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Recipes for dessert\n| Difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[File:CookbookDatebar.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}| [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|Cuisine of the United States]] | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Dessert]]\n\n'''Date bars''' have crumbly upper and lower surfaces with a [[Cookbook:Date|date]] filling in the middle. Also see the [[Cookbook:Date Squares|Date Squares]] recipe.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*3 cups (1 [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]]) cut-up [[Cookbook:Date|dates]]\n*1½ cup water\n*¼ cup [[Cookbook:Shortening|shortening]]\n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] or [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n*1¾ cup [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n*1½ cup quick-cooking [[Cookbook:Oatmeal|oatmeal]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n#Mix the dates, sugar, and water in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]].\n#Cook over low heat, stirring constantly for about 10 minutes or until thickened. Cool.\n#[[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] together the butter, shortening, and brown sugar in a separate container.\n#Mix the flour, salt, baking soda, and oats into the crumble crust mix.\n#Grease a 13x9-inch pan.\n#Evenly press half of the crumble mixture into the bottom of the pan.\n#Spread the date filling on top.\n#Evenly place remaining crumble mixture into the pan, pressing lightly.\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 25 to 30 minutes at [[Cookbook:Oven temperatures|400°F]], or until light brown.\n#Cut into bars while still warm.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for cookies]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using date]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with images]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes for bars]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Date Bars","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"¼ cup white granulated 